> Stringifying a parsed path that has a parameter name followed by text starting with an astral Unicode character that is an identifier continuation incorrectly fails to quote the parameter name, breaking parse/stringify round-trip.

So the problem is when you have a parameter like `:name` followed by text that starts with an astral ID_Continue character, like `:name𝐀`. But in the parse, the `𝐀` got included in the param name instead of being separate text.

Let me look at the parsing more carefully. The param is `:name` and then text starts with `𝐀`. But in my test, it parsed `name𝐀suffix` as a single param name.

Wait, let me re-read the parsing code:

```typescript
if (value === ":" || value === "*") {
    const type = value === ":" ? "param" : "wildcard";
    let name = "";

    if (ID_START.test(chars[index])) {
        do {
            name += chars[index++];
        } while (ID_CONTINUE.test(chars[index]));
